speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there has been discussion among the Parties. I think you will find that there is unanimous consent for the following motion. I move:
That on Thursday, September 3, 1987, the hours of sitting and business of the House shall be as set out in Standing Orders in relation to a Friday sitting day;
And that when the House adjourns Thursday, September 3, 1987, it shall stand adjourned until two o'clock p.m. Wednesday, September 9, 1987.
